  "semantic_fragments": [
    {
      "fragment_type": "scope_limitation",
      "content": "The Infrared Forehead Thermometer is intended for the intermittent measurement of body temperature from the forehead skin surface on people of all ages. It can be used by consumers in the household environment and by health care providers. And PT3SBT can transmit the temperature to a smart device with Bluetooth.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "预期用途",
        "额温枪",
        "体温测量",
        "蓝牙",
        "家用",
        "医疗机构"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "Infrared Forehead Thermometer",
        "PT3SBT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "According to the risk management plan, risk management group has been finished the risk analysis, evaluation, and take the control measures. Now, the device has been in prototype phase, risk control measures have been implemented. The objective of this review is to take a complete evaluation on risk control measures and residual risk.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "风险管理计划",
        "风险分析",
        "风险控制措施",
        "残余风险",
        "原型阶段"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "风险管理计划",
        "风险控制措施验证报告"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "Signification of Abbreviations: RE=Risk Evaluation; S=Severity (1 Negligible; 2 Minor; 3 Serious; 4 Critical; 5 Catastrophic); P=The probability of a harm occurring (1 Few; 2 Improbable; 3 Remote; 4 Occasional; 5 Probable; 6 Frequent); R=Risk NO.; ACC=Acceptable; NACC=Unacceptable; PRM=Plan of Risk control measure(s); NH=New hazard generated; N/A=Not apply; Y=Yes; N=No; AFAP=As far as possible without adversely affecting the benefit-risk ratio.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "缩写定义",
        "严重性分级",
        "发生概率分级",
        "风险评价准则"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "风险评价准则",
        "风险矩阵"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "Please find the document Risk Management Plan (IFT-FXJH01 V1.0) for the risk acceptance criteria.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk acceptance criteria",
        "risk management plan",
        "reference document"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "IFT-FXJH01 V1.0",
        "Risk Management Plan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "In summary, all individual risks are acceptable after implementation of risk control measures. According to ISO 14971:2019 section 7.4 \"Benefit-risk analysis: If a residual risk is not judged acceptable using the criteria established in the risk management plan and further risk control is not practicable, the manufacturer may gather and review data and literature to determine if the benefits of the intended use outweigh this residual risk.\" So there is no need to do a risk benefit analysis for above risks.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "residual risk",
        "benefit-risk analysis",
        "ISO 14971:2019",
        "risk acceptance"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "risk management plan",
        "risk controls"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "Residual risk evaluation and conclusion: According to the risk acceptance table, all single residual risks are in the 'Acceptable' area. The distribution of all the residual risks: R56 is at probability 3/severity 1; R19,R25,R29,R30,R31,R34,R35,R38,R39,R40,R41,R42,R43,R44,R45,R47,R48,R49,R52,R53,R55 are at probability 2/severity 3; R23,R36 are at probability 1/severity 2; R9,R10,R11,R12,R13,R15,R16,R17,R18,R20,R21,R22,R24,R26,R27,R28,R32,R33,R37,R46,R50,R51,R54,R57 are at probability 1/severity 3; R1,R2,R3,R4,R5,R6,R7,R8,R14 are at probability 1/severity 4. Less than 1/2 of the overall residual risks are in the higher severity regions or in the higher probability regions. The clusters of all the residual risks are not borderline. So the overall residual risks are also acceptable.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "residual risk evaluation",
        "overall residual risk",
        "risk matrix",
        "acceptability conclusion"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "risk acceptance table",
        "risk management plan"
      ]
    }
